WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.387
These four are quieter.

2
00:00:01.387 --> 00:00:05.701
Two tools on one setting flip it back
and forth while both report success,

3
00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:10.087
and the fix is the ownership rule,
checked inside every changing playbook.

4
00:00:10.087 --> 00:00:13.467
Public Galaxy content can
change under you between runs,

5
00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:17.206
so pull collections from a reviewed
source, pin exact versions,

6
00:00:17.206 --> 00:00:21.088
verify them, and keep that list as
your software bill of materials.

7
00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:24.867
Running everything as root gives
every mistake root's reach,

8
00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:27.437
so escalate only on
the tasks that need it.

9
00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:32.300
And commands that report a change every
time turn drift reports into noise.

10
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.900
Run each playbook twice in test, and
the second run should change nothing.

11
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.220
Now, how to adopt all of this.
